  "description": "New Hampshire's 1st Congressional District seat is open after incumbent Democrat Chris Pappas announced he would run for U.S. Senate rather than seek re-election. The district, which covers southeastern New Hampshire including Manchester, the Seacoast, and the Lakes Region, is a competitive swing seat that voted for Kamala Harris by two points in 2024. The Democratic primary features a crowded field of seven candidates including former Obama administration official Maura Sullivan, former Portsmouth city councilor Stefany Shaheen (daughter of U.S. Sen. Jeanne Shaheen), and several state and local officials. On the Republican side, state representative Brian Cole and Bedford Republican Committee vice chair Melissa Bailey are competing in their primary. The September 8, 2026 primary will determine the general election matchups.",
